y, carbohydrates are included in parenteral nutrition, with specific daily intake recommendations to prevent complications such as hyperglycemia.\n\nCarbohydrates are also relevant in the context of surgical patients, where they are recommended for intake up to two hours before surgery to alleviate discomfort and anxiety. Furthermore, they are discussed as a nutritional strategy to improve glycemic control and reduce insulin resistance in surgical patients.\n\nWhile carbohydrates are essential, certain types, particularly those with a high glycemic index, should be limited in cases of hypertriglyceridemia. They can also affect conditions like dumping syndrome, especially rapidly absorbed carbohydrates that may lead to hypoglycemia. \n\nOverall, HIDRATOS DE CARBONO are a fundamental component of a balanced diet, contributing to energy storage, athletic performance, and overall health, while requiring careful management in specific medical contexts.\",43\r\n9348,FÓRMULAS RICAS EN GRASA,Fat-rich formulas designed for patients with diabetes to improve metabolic control and manage postprandial glucose levels.,8\r\n9688,MALTODEXTRINAS,\"Maltodextrins are carbohydrate polymers and polysaccharides that serve multiple purposes in the food and beverage industry. They are primarily used as food additives and are produced from starch through a process of partial hydrolysis. In sports drinks, maltodextrins play a crucial role by providing energy and enhancing the absorption of fluids. Additionally, they are significant in the digestion process, contributing to the overall nutritional value of various products.\",5\r\n14385,BEBIDAS DEPORTIVAS,\"BEBIDAS DEPORTIVAS, or sports drinks, are specially designed beverages intended for athletes to maintain proper hydroelectrolytic balance during physical activity. These drinks provide essential hydration and energy, supporting athletes in their performance and endurance while engaging in sports or exercise.\",7\r\n9708,TEST DEL ALIENTO,\"